A taplo `#:schema` directive before the header comment is skipped, and is never a key's comment either.
A comment block that runs on from the header comment (its later paragraphs) belongs to the header, so the first key's line range starts at the key.
== args
input/a.toml
input/b.toml
== file input/a.toml
#:schema https://example.com/schema.json
# Tool configuration.
#
# Second paragraph, still part of the header comment.
[tool]
name = "x"
== file input/b.toml
#:schema https://example.com/schema.json
[tool]
name = "x"
== stdout
input/a.toml (6 lines)
Tool configuration.
[L5-L6] [tool]

input/b.toml (3 lines)
[L2-L3] [tool]
== stderr
== exit 0
